# The generated layer and the kubeconfig beside it. The layer is derived from
# the templates and from an apply's variables, so a committed copy would be a
# second answer to a question the templates already answer; the kubeconfig
# points at one cluster and belongs to one operator.
generated/

# The lock file is not ignored. It is what makes two applies resolve the
# same provider versions, and a stack whose providers drift between applies
# is a stack whose plan cannot be trusted; it is committed at the first init
# and updated on purpose, with -upgrade.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!example.tfvars
